/* ============================================================================
   Chagas disease / Chronic Chagas Cardiomyopathy (CCC)
   Quantitative Systems Pharmacology mechanistic map
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Organising idea (read this before reading the graph)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Four randomised trials in this disease produced four results that look
   mutually contradictory, and every one of them is a statement about a
   DIFFERENT TIME-SCALE.  This map is drawn so that the three time-scales are
   three physically separate objects, and so that each trial's result can be
   read off the structure rather than argued about.

     TIME-SCALE 1 — KILLING, hours to days.
       Benznidazole and posaconazole both drive circulating trypomastigotes
       below the qPCR limit within weeks.  STOP-CHAGAS: PCR negativity at day
       30 was 93.3% on posaconazole and 89.7% on benznidazole — posaconazole
       was the BETTER drug on this time-scale.
       (cluster cl_pd_tryp, edges KILL_REP_*)

     TIME-SCALE 2 — THE RESERVOIR, weeks to months.
       A subset of intracellular amastigotes enters spontaneous, non-replicating
       dormancy.  Dormant parasites are drug-TOLERANT, not drug-resistant: they
       are missed by any agent whose target is only required during growth.
       They wake stochastically with a mean latency of order two months.
       Posaconazole's target (CYP51 / ergosterol biosynthesis) is a GROWTH
       requirement, so its dormant-kill rate is ~0.  Benznidazole's target is
       not: TcNTR-1 reduces the nitroimidazole to reactive glyoxal/nitroso
       species that form DNA adducts in a cell that is not dividing.
       That single asymmetry — one rate constant, KILL_DORM — is the whole
       explanation of STOP-CHAGAS day 180 (posaconazole 13.3%, benznidazole
       86.7%) and of CHAGASAZOL.
       (cluster cl_parasite: P_DORM_* nodes and the k_dorm / k_wake edges)

     TIME-SCALE 3 — REMODELLING, years to decades, AND SELF-SUSTAINING.
       Myocardial damage is driven by a sum of two terms.  One is proportional
       to parasite/antigen load.  The other — fibrosis raising wall stress
       raising fibrosis, autoantibody raised by released cardiac myosin which
       is itself released by autoantibody-driven damage, microvascular spasm
       causing ischaemia causing more spasm — contains no parasite term at all
       and is AUTOCATALYTIC.  The parasite-attributable fraction of the
       instantaneous damage rate therefore FALLS with time since infection, not
       because the parasite leaves, but because the denominator grows.
       (clusters cl_fibrosis, cl_autoimm, cl_microvasc — every one of the three
       loops marked LOOP+ closes without passing through a parasite node.)

   The three trials then read directly off the map:

     BENDITA  (benznidazole 2 vs 4 vs 8 weeks: 83% / 89% / 89%)
       Cure is not an integral of exposure.  It is the question of whether the
       total residual burden was pushed below the level at which the host
       adaptive response finishes the job on its own (node STERILISE).  Once
       below it, further weeks add only the two toxicity hazards, which is why
       the 2-week arm had 0% discontinuation and the 8-week arm did not.

     STOP-CHAGAS / CHAGASAZOL
       Potency against the replicating pool and cure are different endpoints
       separated by one node (P_DORM_H).  A more potent drug that cannot reach
       that node cannot cure at any duration.

     BENEFIT (PCR conversion 66.2% vs 33.5%; clinical HR 0.93, CI 0.81-1.07)
       Enrolment required ESTABLISHED cardiomyopathy, i.e. patients already
       deep into time-scale 3, where the parasite-attributable fraction of the
       damage rate has decayed to a few per cent.  Removing the parasite
       removes what it is attributable for.  The null is a PREDICTION of this
       structure, not a failure of the aetiological hypothesis — and the map
       makes the discriminating experiment obvious, because the same edge that
       is nearly inert at age 55 carries almost all of the damage at age 25.

   A fourth, independent structural claim is made about how patients die.
   Arrhythmic death is NOT driven by the amount of fibrosis but by its SPATIAL
   HETEROGENEITY and by sympathetic denervation (node SCAR_HET, node SYMP_DEN,
   which is why arrhythmia severity tracks MIBG defect extent and not perfusion
   defect extent), whereas pump-failure death is driven by ejection fraction.
   These are two different nodes with two different hazards, and they COMPETE:
   suppressing arrhythmic death with amiodarone or an ICD converts sudden
   deaths into later pump-failure deaths, so the all-cause benefit is far
   smaller than the mode-specific benefit.  Annual rates anchoring this:
   all-cause 7.9%, heart failure 3.5%, sudden 2.6%, stroke 0.4%.

   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Reading conventions
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     solid arrow          = activation / flux / promotion
     tee (odiamond head)  = inhibition / suppression / removal
     dashed               = slow, cumulative, or irreversible process
     bold red             = a step with NO reverse edge anywhere in the graph
                            (irreversible: neuronal loss, replacement fibrosis,
                            conduction tissue loss, aneurysm)
     LOOP+ label          = a positive feedback that closes without a parasite
     double octagon       = measured clinical or trial endpoint
     note shape           = a numerical anchor taken from a named trial

   Node count 231, edge count 397, clusters 30.
   ============================================================================ */

digraph CHAGAS_QSP {
  graph [rankdir=TB, splines=true, nodesep=0.30, ranksep=0.62, fontname="Helvetica",
         fontsize=11, compound=true, bgcolor="white", labelloc="t", fontcolor="#111111",
         label=<<B>Chagas Disease / Chronic Chagas Cardiomyopathy — QSP mechanistic map</B><BR/>
                <FONT POINT-SIZE="10">three time-scales (killing · reservoir · remodelling), three trial paradoxes, one structure</FONT>>];
  node  [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9,
         fillcolor="#F4F6F8", color="#8899AA", penwidth=1.0, margin="0.07,0.04"];
  edge  [color="#667788", penwidth=1.0, arrowsize=0.62, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=7.5];

  /* ---------- 1. TRANSMISSION AND ACUTE PHASE ---------------------------- */
  subgraph cluster_vector {
    label="1 · Transmission routes and inoculum"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#FFF8E7"; color="#D6B86A"; fontsize=11;
    VECTOR   [label="Triatomine vector\n(Triatoma infestans,\nRhodnius prolixus)", fillcolor="#FDF0C8"];
    FAECES   [label="Metacyclic trypomastigotes\nin vector faeces"];
    BITE     [label="Bite-site / mucosal\ninoculation"];
    ORAL     [label="Oral transmission\n(açaí, sugarcane juice)\nhigh inoculum", fillcolor="#FDF0C8"];
    CONGEN   [label="Congenital transmission\n(~4.7% of seropositive\npregnancies)"];
    TRANSF   [label="Transfusion /\norgan transplant"];
    REINF    [label="Repeated domestic\nre-exposure\n(inoculum load)"];
    INOC     [label="Effective inoculum\nN0"];
    VECTOR->FAECES; FAECES->BITE; BITE->INOC; ORAL->INOC; CONGEN->INOC; TRANSF->INOC;
    VECTOR->REINF; REINF->INOC [style=dashed];
  }

  subgraph cluster_acute {
    label="2 · Acute phase (weeks-months)"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#FFF1F1"; color="#D89898"; fontsize=11;
    ACUTE    [label="Acute infection\n(~1% clinically apparent)"];
    PATENT   [label="Patent parasitaemia\n10e3-10e5 par-eq/mL"];
    CHAGOMA  [label="Chagoma / Romaña sign"];
    ACMYO    [label="Acute myocarditis\n(rarely fatal, <5%)"];
    SEROCONV [label="Seroconversion\nanti-T. cruzi IgG"];
    CTLPRIME [label="CD8+ CTL priming\n(trans-sialidase epitopes)"];
    CONTROL  [label="Immune control\nof parasitaemia\n(NOT clearance)", fillcolor="#F6DADA"];
    ACUTE->PATENT; PATENT->CHAGOMA; PATENT->ACMYO; PATENT->SEROCONV; PATENT->CTLPRIME;
    CTLPRIME->CONTROL; SEROCONV->CONTROL;
  }

  /* ---------- 3. PARASITE COMPARTMENTS: THE RESERVOIR --------------------- */
  subgraph cluster_parasite {
    label="3 · Parasite compartments — replicating vs DORMANT reservoir (the model's central structure)";
    style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#EAF4FF"; color="#6699CC"; fontsize=11;
    P_BLOOD  [label="P_BLOOD\ncirculating trypomastigotes\n(chronic: 0.1-10 par-eq/mL)", fillcolor="#CFE4FA"];
    P_REP_H  [label="P_REP_H\nREPLICATING amastigotes\nin cardiomyocytes", fillcolor="#CFE4FA"];
    P_REP_X  [label="P_REP_X\nreplicating amastigotes\nGI smooth muscle · skeletal\nmuscle · adipose", fillcolor="#CFE4FA"];
    P_DORM_H [label="P_DORM_H\nDORMANT amastigotes (heart)\nnon-replicating · drug-TOLERANT", fillcolor="#9CC6EE", penwidth=2.2, color="#1F5C99"];
    P_DORM_X [label="P_DORM_X\nDORMANT amastigotes\n(extracardiac reservoir)", fillcolor="#9CC6EE", penwidth=2.2, color="#1F5C99"];
    NEST     [label="Amastigote pseudocyst\n(nest) rupture"];
    KDORM    [label="k_dorm\nentry into dormancy\n~0.02 /day"];
    KWAKE    [label="k_wake\nstochastic awakening\n~0.015 /day (mean ~67 d)", fillcolor="#CFE4FA"];
    ANTIGEN  [label="ANTIGEN\npersistent T. cruzi antigen\n(GPI-mucin, trans-sialidase,\nshed and long-lived)", fillcolor="#CFE4FA"];
    TISSUE_PCR [label="Tissue PCR positive in\n~60-100% of CCC hearts\ndespite <1 nest / 100 fields", shape=note, fillcolor="#FFFFFF"];
    STERILISE [label="STERILISE\nhost adaptive response finishes\nclearance if total burden falls\nbelow extinction scale", fillcolor="#9CC6EE", penwidth=2.2, color="#1F5C99"];
    P_BLOOD->P_REP_H; P_BLOOD->P_REP_X;
    P_REP_H->NEST; NEST->P_BLOOD [label="release"];
    P_REP_H->KDORM; KDORM->P_DORM_H [style=dashed];
    P_REP_X->KDORM; KDORM->P_DORM_X [style=dashed];
    P_DORM_H->KWAKE; P_DORM_X->KWAKE; KWAKE->P_REP_H; KWAKE->P_REP_X;
    P_REP_H->ANTIGEN; NEST->ANTIGEN; P_DORM_H->ANTIGEN [style=dashed];
    P_REP_H->TISSUE_PCR [style=dotted, arrowhead=none];
    P_REP_H->STERILISE [style=dashed]; P_DORM_H->STERILISE [style=dashed];
    P_REP_X->STERILISE [style=dashed]; P_DORM_X->STERILISE [style=dashed];
    CONTROL->P_BLOOD [lhead=cluster_parasite, style=dashed];
  }

  subgraph cluster_strain {
    label="4 · Parasite genetic background (DTU)"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#F2EAFB"; color="#A98BD0"; fontsize=11;
    DTU_I    [label="TcI\nNorthern S. America, Colombia\nMexico, Central America"];
    DTU_II   [label="TcII / TcV / TcVI\nSouthern Cone\nBrazil, Argentina, Bolivia"];
    TROPISM  [label="Tissue tropism\n(cardiac vs digestive)"];
    BZN_SENS [label="Intrinsic benznidazole\nsusceptibility (EC50 multiplier)"];
    GEO_ANCH [label="BENEFIT geographic interaction:\nOR for PCR conversion at >=5 y\nBrazil 1.87 · Arg/Bol 2.79 ·\nCol/ElSal 0.96  (p<0.001 interaction)", shape=note, fillcolor="#FFFFFF"];
    DTU_I->BZN_SENS [label="lower"]; DTU_II->BZN_SENS [label="higher"];
    DTU_I->TROPISM; DTU_II->TROPISM;
    BZN_SENS->GEO_ANCH [style=dotted, arrowhead=none];
  }

  /* ---------- 5-8. IMMUNITY ---------------------------------------------- */
  subgraph cluster_innate {
    label="5 · Innate sensing and macrophage activation"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#EAF7EE"; color="#77B58C"; fontsize=11;
    TLR2     [label="TLR2 / TLR4\n(GPI anchors of mucins)"];
    TLR9     [label="TLR9\n(parasite CpG DNA)"];
    NLRP3    [label="NLRP3 inflammasome\n→ caspase-1"];
    MYD88    [label="MyD88 → NF-kB"];
    MPHI     [label="MPHI\nactivated macrophage\n(M1 polarised)", fillcolor="#CDE9D7"];
    ROSNO    [label="ROS / iNOS → NO\nperoxynitrite"];
    MITO     [label="Mitochondrial dysfunction\n(cardiomyocyte)"];
    ANTIGEN->TLR2; ANTIGEN->TLR9; P_REP_H->NLRP3;
    TLR2->MYD88; TLR9->MYD88; MYD88->MPHI; NLRP3->MPHI;
    MPHI->ROSNO; ROSNO->MITO;
  }

  subgraph cluster_adaptive {
    label="6 · Adaptive immunity — protective and pathogenic at once"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#EAF7EE"; color="#77B58C"; fontsize=11;
    TH1      [label="TH1\nIFN-g+ CD4 / CD8 effector\ncardiac infiltrate", fillcolor="#CDE9D7"];
    TH17     [label="Th17 (IL-17A)"];
    TREG     [label="TREG\nFoxP3+ regulatory T cells\n(REDUCED in severe CCC)", fillcolor="#CDE9D7"];
    CTL      [label="CD8+ cytotoxic T cell\n(perforin/granzyme)"];
    EXHAUST  [label="T-cell exhaustion\n(PD-1+, CD28-, terminal\neffector accumulation)"];
    KILL_INF [label="Killing of INFECTED\ncardiomyocyte\n(protective AND damaging)", fillcolor="#CDE9D7"];
    BYSTAND  [label="Bystander killing of\nUNINFECTED myocytes"];
    ANTIGEN->TH1; ANTIGEN->TH17; P_REP_H->CTL;
    TH1->CTL; CTL->KILL_INF; CTL->BYSTAND;
    TREG->TH1 [arrowhead=odiamond]; TREG->TH17 [arrowhead=odiamond];
    TH1->EXHAUST [style=dashed]; EXHAUST->CTL [arrowhead=odiamond, style=dashed];
    KILL_INF->P_REP_H [arrowhead=odiamond];
    MPHI->P_REP_H [arrowhead=odiamond, label="phagocytic\nkilling"];
  }

  subgraph cluster_autoimm {
    label="7 · Molecular mimicry and functional autoantibodies  (LOOP+ — closes without a parasite)";
    style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#FDEDF5"; color="#CC7FAA"; fontsize=11;
    B13      [label="T. cruzi B13 protein"];
    CHA_AG   [label="T. cruzi Cha antigen"];
    MYOSIN   [label="Cardiac myosin heavy chain\n(released by myocyte death)", fillcolor="#F8D6E7"];
    MIMIC    [label="Molecular mimicry\ncross-reactive T / B clones"];
    AAB_B1   [label="Anti-beta1-adrenoceptor\nagonist autoantibody", fillcolor="#F8D6E7"];
    AAB_M2   [label="Anti-M2-muscarinic\nautoantibody", fillcolor="#F8D6E7"];
    AAB_RIB  [label="Anti-ribosomal P /\nanti-Cha antibodies"];
    CAMP_STIM[label="Chronic beta1 stimulation\n→ cAMP / CaMKII\n→ Ca2+ leak"];
    EAD      [label="Early afterdepolarisations\ntriggered activity"];
    B13->MIMIC; CHA_AG->MIMIC; MYOSIN->MIMIC;
    MIMIC->AAB_B1; MIMIC->AAB_M2; MIMIC->AAB_RIB;
    AAB_B1->CAMP_STIM; CAMP_STIM->EAD;
  }

  subgraph cluster_cyto {
    label="8 · Cytokine / chemokine network"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#EAF7EE"; color="#77B58C"; fontsize=11;
    IFNG     [label="IFN-gamma", fillcolor="#CDE9D7"];
    TNFA     [label="TNF-alpha", fillcolor="#CDE9D7"];
    IL1B     [label="IL-1beta"];
    IL6      [label="IL-6"];
    IL10     [label="IL-10 (regulatory)"];
    TGFB     [label="TGF-beta1", fillcolor="#CDE9D7"];
    CCL2     [label="CCL2 / CCL5 / CXCL9-10\nchemokine gradient"];
    CCR5     [label="CCR5+ monocyte and\nT-cell recruitment"];
    IL17     [label="IL-17A (protective in\nexperimental models)"];
    TH1->IFNG; MPHI->TNFA; NLRP3->IL1B; MPHI->IL6; TREG->IL10; MPHI->TGFB; TH1->TGFB;
    IFNG->MPHI [label="amplify"]; TNFA->CCL2; IFNG->CCL2; CCL2->CCR5; CCR5->MPHI;
    IL10->TNFA [arrowhead=odiamond]; IL10->IFNG [arrowhead=odiamond];
    TH17->IL17; IL17->MPHI [arrowhead=odiamond, style=dashed];
  }

  /* ---------- 9-11. MYOCARDIAL TISSUE ------------------------------------ */
  subgraph cluster_myocyte {
    label="9 · Cardiomyocyte injury and loss"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#FFF1E6"; color="#D9A06A"; fontsize=11;
    CMYO     [label="CMYO\nviable cardiomyocyte mass", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    APOP     [label="Apoptosis / necroptosis"];
    NECRO    [label="Necrosis (focal myocytolysis)"];
    HYPER    [label="Compensatory hypertrophy\nof surviving myocytes"];
    CA_HAND  [label="Ca2+ handling defect\nSERCA2a down, NCX up"];
    CONTR    [label="Contractility\n(regional then global)", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    MYO_REL  [label="Release of cardiac myosin,\ntroponin, mitochondrial DAMPs", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    TNI      [label="hs-troponin I elevation\n(chronic, low-grade)"];
    KILL_INF->APOP; BYSTAND->APOP; ROSNO->NECRO; MITO->APOP; TNFA->APOP; MITO->CA_HAND;
    APOP->CMYO [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    NECRO->CMYO [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    CMYO->CONTR; CA_HAND->CONTR [arrowhead=odiamond];
    APOP->MYO_REL; NECRO->MYO_REL; MYO_REL->TNI;
    MYO_REL->MYOSIN [color="#CC3377", penwidth=1.8, label="LOOP+  autoantigen\nsupply is DOWNSTREAM\nof the damage"];
    CMYO->HYPER [style=dashed]; HYPER->CONTR [style=dashed];
  }

  subgraph cluster_fibrosis {
    label="10 · Fibroblast activation and ECM  (LOOP+ — autocatalytic, no parasite term)";
    style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#FFF1E6"; color="#D9A06A"; fontsize=11;
    FIBRO    [label="Resident cardiac fibroblast"];
    MFB      [label="MFB\nactivated myofibroblast\n(alpha-SMA+)", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    COL13    [label="COL\ncollagen I / III deposition\n(interstitial + replacement)", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    MMPS     [label="MMP-2 / MMP-9"];
    TIMP     [label="TIMP-1 / TIMP-2"];
    LOX      [label="LOX cross-linking\n(stiffening)"];
    SCAR     [label="Replacement scar\n(irreversible)", color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    SCAR_HET [label="SCAR_HET\nborder-zone / grey-zone\nHETEROGENEITY index\n(NOT total fibrosis)", fillcolor="#F2B98A", penwidth=2.2, color="#B03030"];
    LGE      [label="LGE mass on CMR\n(76.1% prevalence,\n15.2 +/- 16.5 g)"];
    STIFF    [label="Diastolic stiffness"];
    TGFB->MFB; TNFA->FIBRO; FIBRO->MFB; MFB->COL13; MFB->TIMP;
    TIMP->MMPS [arrowhead=odiamond]; MMPS->COL13 [arrowhead=odiamond]; COL13->LOX; LOX->STIFF;
    COL13->SCAR [style=dashed, color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    SCAR->SCAR_HET; COL13->SCAR_HET; NECRO->SCAR_HET [label="patchy\nmyocytolysis"];
    SCAR->LGE; COL13->LGE;
    MFB->TGFB [color="#CC7700", penwidth=1.8, label="LOOP+ autocrine"];
    COL13->STIFF;
  }

  subgraph cluster_microvasc {
    label="11 · Microvascular dysfunction  (LOOP+)"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#FFF1E6"; color="#D9A06A"; fontsize=11;
    ET1      [label="ET1\nendothelin-1", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    THROMBX  [label="Thromboxane A2\nplatelet aggregation"];
    SPASM    [label="Microvascular spasm\ncapillary rarefaction"];
    CFR      [label="Coronary flow reserve\nreduced"];
    ISCH     [label="Focal ischaemia\n(perfusion defect, often\nREVERSIBLE on scintigraphy)", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    ENDOTH   [label="Endothelial dysfunction\nNO bioavailability down"];
    P_REP_H->ET1; TNFA->ET1; ET1->SPASM; THROMBX->SPASM; SPASM->CFR;
    CFR->ISCH [arrowhead=odiamond]; ISCH->NECRO; ISCH->ENDOTH; ENDOTH->ET1 [color="#CC7700", penwidth=1.8, label="LOOP+"];
  }

  /* ---------- 12-14. ELECTRICAL AND AUTONOMIC ---------------------------- */
  subgraph cluster_autonomic {
    label="12 · Autonomic denervation — early and irreversible"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#EFEFFA"; color="#8A8AC8"; fontsize=11;
    INTRACARD [label="Intracardiac parasympathetic\nganglion neurons"];
    PSYM_DEN [label="PSYM_DEN\nvagal denervation\n(HRV loss, chronotropic\nincompetence)", fillcolor="#D6D6F0", color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    SYMP_DEN [label="SYMP_DEN\nregional SYMPATHETIC denervation\n(123I-MIBG defect)", fillcolor="#C4C4EA", penwidth=2.2, color="#B03030"];
    DENERV_SUPER [label="Denervation supersensitivity\n(regional beta-receptor up)"];
    MIBG_ANCH [label="Arrhythmia severity tracks\nMIBG DEFECT EXTENT,\nnot perfusion defect extent", shape=note, fillcolor="#FFFFFF"];
    PSYM_DEN_L [label="Loss of baroreflex\nbuffering"];
    INTRACARD->PSYM_DEN [color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    CTL->INTRACARD [arrowhead=odiamond]; ISCH->SYMP_DEN; CTL->SYMP_DEN [arrowhead=odiamond];
    SYMP_DEN->DENERV_SUPER; PSYM_DEN->PSYM_DEN_L;
    SYMP_DEN->MIBG_ANCH [style=dotted, arrowhead=none];
    AAB_M2->PSYM_DEN [style=dashed];
  }

  subgraph cluster_conduction {
    label="13 · Conduction system — the earliest clinical marker"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#EFEFFA"; color="#8A8AC8"; fontsize=11;
    RBB      [label="Right bundle branch\n(thin, single blood supply,\nmost vulnerable)"];
    LAF      [label="Left anterior fascicle"];
    AVN      [label="AV node / His bundle"];
    SAN      [label="Sinus node"];
    RBBB     [label="RBBB + LAFB\n(classic Chagas ECG signature)", fillcolor="#D6D6F0"];
    AVB      [label="2nd / 3rd degree AV block"];
    SSS      [label="Sick sinus syndrome\nbradyarrhythmia"];
    LOWQRS   [label="Low QRS voltage\n(Rassi 2 points)"];
    QRSD     [label="QRS duration >=120 ms\n(cardiomyopathy definition)"];
    SCAR->RBB [color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0]; SCAR->LAF [color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    SCAR->AVN; SCAR->SAN; RBB->RBBB; LAF->RBBB; AVN->AVB; SAN->SSS;
    RBBB->QRSD; SCAR->LOWQRS; PSYM_DEN->SSS [style=dashed];
  }

  subgraph cluster_arrhythmia {
    label="14 · Arrhythmia substrate — heterogeneity, not amount"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#EFEFFA"; color="#8A8AC8"; fontsize=11;
    REENTRY  [label="Anatomical re-entry circuits\n(surviving myocyte bundles\nthrough scar)"];
    PVC      [label="Frequent PVCs"];
    NSVT     [label="NSVT on 24 h Holter\n(Rassi 3 points)", fillcolor="#D6D6F0"];
    SVT      [label="Sustained monomorphic VT"];
    VF       [label="VF / electromechanical\ndissociation"];
    TWA      [label="Microvolt T-wave alternans\n(repolarisation instability)"];
    SCAR_HET->REENTRY [penwidth=2.0]; SYMP_DEN->REENTRY [penwidth=2.0]; DENERV_SUPER->PVC;
    EAD->PVC; REENTRY->NSVT; PVC->NSVT; NSVT->SVT; SVT->VF; SCAR_HET->TWA;
  }

  /* ---------- 15-17. PUMP, NEUROHORMONAL, THROMBOEMBOLIC ----------------- */
  subgraph cluster_remodel {
    label="15 · LV remodelling and haemodynamics"; style="rounded,filled"; fillcolor="#FFF1E6"; color="#D9A06A"; fontsize=11;
    EDV      [label="LV end-diastolic volume", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    ESV      [label="LV end-systolic volume", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    EF       [label="EF\nleft ventricular\nejection fraction", fillcolor="#F2B98A", penwidth=2.0];
    WALL_STRESS [label="WALL_STRESS\nLaplace  sigma = P.r / 2h", fillcolor="#FAD9BC"];
    APEX_THIN[label="APEX_THIN\napical thinning\n(thinnest wall, highest\nstress, watershed perfusion)", color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    ANEUR    [label="Apical aneurysm\n(~50% of CCC)", fillcolor="#FAD9BC", color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    CO       [label="Cardiac output"];
    LVFP     [label="LV filling pressure"];
    CONGEST  [label="Pulmonary and systemic\ncongestion"];
    NYHA     [label="NYHA class III/IV\n(Rassi 5 points)"];
    CMEG     [label="Cardiomegaly on CXR\n(Rassi 5 points)"];
    CONTR->ESV [arrowhead=odiamond]; CMYO->CONTR; ESV->EF [arrowhead=odiamond]; EDV->EF;
    CMYO->EDV [arrowhead=odiamond, label="loss → dilatation"];
    EDV->WALL_STRESS; STIFF->LVFP; EF->CO;
    WALL_STRESS->APEX_THIN [penwidth=1.6]; APEX_THIN->ANEUR [color="#B03030", penwidth=2.0];
    APEX_THIN->WALL_STRESS [color="#CC7700", penwidth=1.8, label="LOOP+ thinner wall\n→ more stress"];
    LVFP->CONGEST; CONGEST->NYHA; EDV->CMEG; CO->NYHA [arrowhead=odiamond];
    WALL_STRESS->APOP [style=dashed];
  }

  subgraph cluster_neuro {
